## 🎯 Day 36 Objective

Day 34 gave us the **register** (what could go wrong). Day 35 gave us the **intake/AIA** (should we build it at all). Day 36 is the **transparency + sign-off layer**: the **Model Card** that documents what a system *actually is*, and the **Responsible AI (RAI) Review Checklist** that a reviewer runs before it ships.

A model card without a review is documentation theater. A review without a model card has nothing to review. Together they're the artifact an auditor, a regulator, or your own future team reaches for when they ask "what is this thing and who said it was OK?"

---

## 🔍 What I Did

- Built a **Model Card template** — a standardized, one-page-per-model spec covering purpose, data, performance, limits, and fairness (extending the Mitchell et al. "Model Cards" pattern for the GenAI era)
- Built a **9-domain RAI Review Checklist** with pass/fail/N-A gates a reviewer can actually run
- Defined **who signs what** (the RACI for a go-live decision)
- Added a **GenAI/LLM-specific supplement** because classic model cards assume a trained classifier, not a foundation-model app
- Mapped both to ISO 42001, EU AI Act Art. 11/13, and NIST AI RMF

